Phasmid: geolocation

What:     A granted page gets locale.geolocation from a provider that
          behaves as stock Chrome's on the claimed OS: nothing before the
          grant, the first fix a seeded 200 to 300 ms after start, altitude,
          heading and speed null. Linux (network provider) stamps the start
          time and re-reports after 2 s; Windows (WinRT) stamps on delivery.
          Without the field the build's network provider runs and fails.
Why:      An ungoogled build cannot reach Google's location service, so a
          granted page gets an error where Google Chrome has a position; an
          instant fix looks like DevTools' override.
Profile:  locale.geolocation.latitude, locale.geolocation.longitude,
          locale.geolocation.accuracy, seed, os.family
Hooks:    services/device/geolocation/location_provider_manager.cc
          LocationProviderManager::InitializeProvider; new
          services/device/geolocation/profile_location_provider.{h,cc};
          services/device/geolocation/BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframe (cross-origin with allow="geolocation"); workers have
          no geolocation
Guard:    tests/guards/locale/geolocation.py

